{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-020",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 20,
  "title": "Job 20",
  "display_title": "Job 20",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 20,
  "sortOrder": 18020,
  "verseCount": 29,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then answered Zophar the Naamathite, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Therefore do my thoughts cause me to answer, and for this I make haste.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "I have heard the check of my reproach, and the spirit of my understanding causeth me to answer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Knowest thou not this of old, since man was placed upon earth,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "That the triumphing of the wicked is short, and the joy of the hypocrite but for a moment?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Though his excellency mount up to the heavens, and his head reach unto the clouds;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Yet he shall perish for ever like his own dung: they which have seen him shall say, Where is he?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "He shall fly away as a dream, and shall not be found: yea, he shall be chased away as a vision of the night.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "The eye also which saw him shall see him no more; neither shall his place any more behold him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "His children shall seek to please the poor, and his hands shall restore their goods.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "His bones are full of the sin of his youth, which shall lie down with him in the dust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Though wickedness be sweet in his mouth, though he hide it under his tongue;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Though he spare it, and forsake it not; but keep it still within his mouth:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Yet his meat in his bowels is turned, it is the gall of asps within him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "He hath swallowed down riches, and he shall vomit them up again: God shall cast them out of his belly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "He shall suck the poison of asps: the viper’s tongue shall slay him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He shall not see the rivers, the floods, the brooks of honey and butter.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "That which he laboured for shall he restore, and shall not swallow it down: according to his substance shall the restitution be, and he shall not rejoice therein.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Because he hath oppressed and hath forsaken the poor; because he hath violently taken away an house which he builded not;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Surely he shall not feel quietness in his belly, he shall not save of that which he desired.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "There shall none of his meat be left; therefore shall no man look for his goods.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "In the fulness of his sufficiency he shall be in straits: every hand of the wicked shall come upon him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "When he is about to fill his belly, God shall cast the fury of his wrath upon him, and shall rain it upon him while he is eating.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "He shall flee from the iron weapon, and the bow of steel shall strike him through.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "It is drawn, and cometh out of the body; yea, the glittering sword cometh out of his gall: terrors are upon him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "All darkness shall be hid in his secret places: a fire not blown shall consume him; it shall go ill with him that is left in his tabernacle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "The heaven shall reveal his iniquity; and the earth shall rise up against him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "The increase of his house shall depart, and his goods shall flow away in the day of his wrath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:20:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "This is the portion of a wicked man from God, and the heritage appointed unto him by God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 20:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:20:29"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
